1
00:01:33,479 --> 00:01:34,520
I'll go cook.

2
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:48,600
Let me help you.

3
00:01:59,440 --> 00:02:01,360
Do you need me to do anything?

4
00:02:08,639 --> 00:02:09,440
Okay.

5
00:02:39,760 --> 00:02:41,090
This looks really good.

6
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:42,090
Have a taste.

7
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:47,530
Did I cook for you often before?

8
00:02:48,880 --> 00:02:49,680
What?

9
00:02:50,880 --> 00:02:53,010
You've been reborn many times, right?

10
00:02:53,079 --> 00:02:54,920
When we were together before,

11
00:02:55,120 --> 00:02:56,450
did I cook for you often?

12
00:03:18,520 --> 00:03:20,480
Aren't you going to have a bite before you go?

13
00:03:20,480 --> 00:03:22,010
No, I have a flight to catch.

14
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:24,240
When I'm not home,

15
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:26,370
look for Pei Ning if you need anything.

16
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:35,920
What are you thinking about?

17
00:03:36,920 --> 00:03:37,520
Nothing.

18
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:39,620
Let me try it first.

19
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:50,120
It's really good.

20
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:52,360
I didn't expect you to be such a good cook.

21
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:55,020
I feel like you could open a private restaurant.

22
00:03:55,320 --> 00:03:56,579
Is it really that good?

23
00:03:57,200 --> 00:03:59,280
I'm serious, it's really delicious.

24
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:01,960
Then try this.

25
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:07,720
Shiya.

26
00:04:09,400 --> 00:04:11,530
I missed out on how good you are before.

27
00:04:11,800 --> 00:04:12,840
But this time,

28
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:15,560
I won't let you go no matter what.

29
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:22,079
Do you want some wine?

30
00:04:22,360 --> 00:04:23,160
I'll go get it.

31
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:24,040
Okay.

32
00:05:10,360 --> 00:05:12,160
Why did you only bring one glass?

33
00:06:14,880 --> 00:06:15,880
I'm sorry,

34
00:06:15,880 --> 00:06:16,680
Pei Song.

35
00:06:17,680 --> 00:06:19,740
Forgive me, but I can't say yes to you.

36
00:06:21,080 --> 00:06:22,320
There are some things

37
00:06:23,480 --> 00:06:25,360
I must face on my own.

38
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,530
Time to take your medicine.

39
00:06:54,280 --> 00:06:55,400
Just leave.

40
00:06:56,480 --> 00:06:57,740
I don't want to see you.

41
00:06:59,960 --> 00:07:02,760
The Pei family doesn't have a descendant like you.

42
00:07:04,320 --> 00:07:06,180
Shiya and I truly love each other.

43
00:07:07,240 --> 00:07:08,280
You're lying.

44
00:07:09,960 --> 00:07:11,760
Don't think just because I'm old

45
00:07:12,240 --> 00:07:13,770
that I don't know anything.

46
00:07:15,240 --> 00:07:16,720
That thing you're making,

47
00:07:17,200 --> 00:07:18,680
the big data AI...

48
00:07:19,720 --> 00:07:21,080
It's impossible to succeed.

49
00:07:21,080 --> 00:07:21,880
Enough!

50
00:07:23,200 --> 00:07:24,240
What do you know?

51
00:07:25,720 --> 00:07:27,240
It's you who

52
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:30,300
never looked at me properly since I was a kid!

53
00:07:30,760 --> 00:07:32,840
I do exactly what my brother does.

54
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:34,600
Why does he get everything?

55
00:07:36,800 --> 00:07:38,320
How am I inferior to him?

56
00:07:39,440 --> 00:07:41,170
Your brother does those things

57
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:42,610
because of his passion.

58
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:44,400
But you?

59
00:07:45,280 --> 00:07:46,940
You just do it out of jealousy.

60
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,600
Your intentions are impure,

61
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:51,330
so naturally, you fail.

62
00:07:51,400 --> 00:07:52,560
Nonsense!

63
00:07:53,440 --> 00:07:54,760
You're just biased!

64
00:07:56,120 --> 00:07:58,120
You'll never surpass your brother.

65
00:08:01,960 --> 00:08:02,880
Say that again.

66
00:08:03,800 --> 00:08:05,800
You'll never surpass your brother.

67
00:08:06,040 --> 00:08:08,500
And I'll never admit you're better than him.

68
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:09,440
The Pei family

69
00:08:09,640 --> 00:08:11,440
only has one grandson, your brother.

70
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:13,170
You don't deserve the name Pei.

71
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:14,360
Say that again!

72
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:16,760
My name is Pei!

73
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:17,880
My name is Pei!

74
00:08:18,320 --> 00:08:19,450
Is my name Pei or not?

75
00:08:19,560 --> 00:08:20,360
My name is Pei.

76
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:21,320
My name is Pei Ning!

77
00:08:21,320 --> 00:08:21,800
Stop!

78
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:37,250
Why are you here?

79
00:08:38,039 --> 00:08:39,840
Do you want to beat your brother?

80
00:08:41,559 --> 00:08:42,600
I'll marry you.

81
00:08:43,120 --> 00:08:44,850
I'll sign a divorce agreement.

82
00:08:45,120 --> 00:08:47,560
Then you record a video of me and send it to Pei Song.

83
00:08:47,560 --> 00:08:48,890
I'll make it clear to him

84
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:50,400
to stop bothering me.

85
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:54,840
Really?

86
00:08:57,840 --> 00:08:58,640
Really.

87
00:09:04,360 --> 00:09:05,160
Okay.

88
00:09:16,560 --> 00:09:17,120
Brother,

89
00:09:17,560 --> 00:09:19,760
just sign this divorce agreement.

90
00:09:20,200 --> 00:09:21,860
Shiya doesn't love you at all.

91
00:09:22,040 --> 00:09:23,000
This time,

92
00:09:24,200 --> 00:09:25,880
I won.

93
00:09:29,560 --> 00:09:31,280
Pei Song, let's get a divorce.

94
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:33,840
Our marriage was just a contract anyway.

95
00:09:33,840 --> 00:09:35,240
Don't come looking for me.

96
00:09:35,240 --> 00:09:36,360
With Pei Ning,

97
00:09:36,560 --> 00:09:37,620
I'll be very happy.

98
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:44,800
Pei Song, let's get a divorce.

99
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:46,920
Our marriage was an agreement in the first place.

100
00:09:46,920 --> 00:09:47,960
Don't come looking for me.

101
00:09:47,960 --> 00:09:49,090
Being with Pei Ning,

102
00:09:49,240 --> 00:09:50,370
I will be very happy.

103
00:09:58,520 --> 00:09:59,080
Don't you think

104
00:09:59,080 --> 00:10:00,520
the encryption method of this code

105
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:02,180
is very similar to Morse code?

106
00:10:02,600 --> 00:10:03,930
The key is the codebook.

107
00:10:04,480 --> 00:10:05,360
An encryption method

108
00:10:05,360 --> 00:10:06,280
can often

109
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:07,940
reveal a person's character.

110
00:10:14,360 --> 00:10:16,220
If you are in danger in the future,

111
00:10:16,280 --> 00:10:18,740
you can use your favorite book as a codebook.

112
00:11:40,640 --> 00:11:41,440
Shiya.

113
00:11:42,880 --> 00:11:43,680
Shiya.
